  "testId": "testClasses.webstore.productDisplayPage.ConfigurableProductDisplayPageTest#configurableProductVerifyWriteAReviewFunctionality",
  "scenario": {
    "summary": "Signed in, on the configurable PDP: opens Write a Review for the shown variant, verifies the review form labels and the required-field messages, submits a review and verifies it is listed on the PDP after a refresh.",
    "steps": [
      "Open the Reviews panel and Write a Review",
      "Verify the product name on the review page",
      "Verify the form labels",
      "Submit empty, verify the required-field messages",
      "Fill rating, headline, review, name and location; submit",
      "Verify the confirmation, close it, cancel",
      "Refresh the PDP, open Reviews and verify the submitted review"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "user",
      "product",
      "review"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "A product review is created for the shown variant (not removed)"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Review page product name equals the shown variant's name",
      "Labels and required messages",
      "Submitted review shown on the PDP"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "dependsOn configurableProductVerifyConfigurableProductEighthVarientDetails.",
      "Class chain, first method captures (user decision 2026-11-04): configurableProductSearchForConfigurableProduct runs first and declares every record need of the chain (product, variant1..variant8); the migrated class keeps the resolved records in class fields and the later methods read them (SkipException DATA_UNAVAILABLE when a field is null), so they declare no product needs of their own. This method reads variant5.variantName: the PDP still shows the variant selected by the inventory method (priority 45), whose name the sheet records as L208 (z-2510006); that value is declared as a source of configurableProductSearchForConfigurableProduct; until the class is migrated, check-hardcoded reports it here.",
      "Review page labels and the required-field messages are UI texts: expected-output (B507, the name label, is masked by the key-name rule). Headline 'Great Purchase', comment 'Value for Money', reviewer name (B500, masked) and location 'Boston, USA' are values the test chooses and types: config. The review itself is created by the test (stateChanges).",
      "DECLARED ACCOUNT (per method): the class signs in once in configurableProductSearchForConfigurableProduct with loginPage.successfullLogin(testClassRetailUsers/configurableProductPDPTest Username, Password; loginAndRegistration!B176/C176) and every later method works in that signed-in session (its cart, wishlist, review). An account lease is held by the declaring method only, so each method declares user = USER_WEBSTORE_REGISTERED {store MaxwellsHardware}, preferred {source: the username source, required: true}, declared at method start with Tda.declareUser (useExisting), as the Selenium quickOrder retail entries. Username/password stay credential sources (masked) the test keeps reading from its own sheet; the scanner recorded them only on the head method, here the same two cells are declared from the test source (the session it reuses).",
      "Store: openWebstoreUrl opens automation_webStoreUrl (atstage: webstore-z10-atstage, the main store MaxwellsHardware), the same store as the Selenium shoppingCart/quickOrder entries and the Playwright pdp entries.",
      "Profile: work/profiles/profile.json (2026-11-01) has no observations for these Selenium cells (profiled false); DB facts from bin/tda rows (2026-11-06) and the approved Playwright pdp entries where cited.",
      "Scanned constant values (locators, report messages, delays, image extension) are framework constants: role config, no need.",
      "migrate: Selenium reads Excel tables through TestData.getMap; there is no swap for Selenium."
    ],
    "confidence": "medium"
  },
  "requires": [
